<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramadan al-Suwayhili</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ramadan Asswehly, Ramadan al-Swehli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramadan">Ramadan</a> al-Suwayhili was a leader of Misrata in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and one of the main figures of the resistance to Italian rule. In 1915 he turned against the Italians at the battle of al-Qardabiya, a heavy defeat for their forces. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> he joined the ruling council of the Tripolitanian Republic, but rivalries among its leaders led to fighting, and he was killed in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramadan-al-suwayhili.jpg" alt="Ramadan al-Suwayhili" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khayr al-Din al-Zirikli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramadan_al-Suwayhili_-_Al-Alam,_V_3,_P_71.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
